This test must compile and run, but its compilation must *also* report a warning:
`Gadget?` and `string?` are annotations on types that are already nullable, which is
the condition C# gives CS8632 for. `run.sh` recompiles it with warnings enabled and
requires the code, so the warning cannot silently go away. The third line is the
value-type `int?`, which is `Nullable<T>` and warns about nothing.
code: NS8632
